// The browse-scale joint itest (contracts/4.1-joint-itest.md): the real
// instances end to end — a real store (openAPIStore), the real module registry
// (module.Open), the real gate resolution (enrich.ResolveGates), the real
// naming composer (naming.Namer), the real browse.Service, and the real
// mountV1Routes behind the synthetic-principal/viewer seam. No mocks between
// joints; the ONLY test-scoped glue is the composer below, a faithful mirror
// of cmd/mellifera/browse_wiring.go built here because package api tests
// cannot import cmd (cmd imports api). Two divergences from the cmd file,
// both deliberate:
//   - the per-pass namer cache is CLEARED at every Corpus pass top — the
//     invariant browse_wiring.go documents (its "CLEARED at every Corpus
//     pass" comment); the contract's gate-flip clause requires the
//     post-drift rebuild to recompose under the CURRENT gates;
//   - SourceInventory is derived from the live registry's metadata-source
//     bindings (the boot-literal catalog's honest analog; cmd ships the
//     same ids as literals at boot).
//
// Subtest ORDER is load-bearing: the first four clauses read the pristine
// fixture; the rename and the gate flip mutate state and run last, each
// asserting the transition its contract clause names.

